.TH OPENCLOUD 1 "2026-11-15" "OpenCloud Desktop 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opencloud \- OpenCloud desktop file synchronization client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opencloud
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opencloud
is the graphical client of OpenCloud. It synchronizes files between an
OpenCloud server and your computer and shows a system tray icon with the
sync status.
.PP
By default the client launches in the background. If another instance is
already running, new invocations are forwarded to it (single instance).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show
Start with the main window visible, or bring a running instance to the front.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.BI \-\-logfile " filename"
Write the log to the given file (use
.B \-
to write to stdout).
.TP
.BI \-\-logdir " name"
Write each sync log output in a new file in the given folder.
.TP
.B \-\-logflush
Flush the log file after every write.
.TP
.B \-\-logdebug
Output debug-level messages in the log.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug mode.
.TP
.B \-\-cmd
Forward all arguments to the command line client (opencloudcmd). This
argument must be the first.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/OpenCloud/opencloud.cfg
Client configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/OpenCloud/
Default local sync folder location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR opencloudcmd (1)
.SH AUTHOR
OpenCloud contributors.
